     9	#     new_rule: 固定两种可见墙色都是真墙；蓝色边框发出 1 像素厚边界射线，红色边框发出 2 像素厚边界射线。
    10	#     mapping_visibility: 颜色到参数的映射在整题内恒定，且每个样例同时出现蓝墙和红墙，让解题者能直接对比。
    11	#   concretization:
    12	#     objects:
    13	#       - 每个输入含 2 个 U/V 形半包围墙组件，形状沿用原题的锯齿臂和 1:1 / 1:2 端点模式。
    14	#       - 两个组件共享同一种填充色，确保差异只能从边框颜色解释。
    15	#       - 其余非背景单点仍是障碍物，保留原题“投影阴影”行为。
    16	#     visual_effect:
    17	#       - 蓝墙输出与原题近似：填充从内部穿过开口，向外在两条细边界射线之间扩散。
    18	#       - 红墙的每条边界射线向填充区域内侧再复制一条平行射线，形成 2 像素厚边界带，因此外放区域明显更窄。
    19	#   behavior_trace:
    20	#     small_example:
    21	#       - 原题：若开口宽约 6 格，则两端各发一条细射线，远处横截面大致保留原本张角。
    22	#       - 变体：同样几何下，红墙两端各多一条紧贴内侧的平行射线，远处横截面会少掉两侧各 1 格。
    23	#       - difference: 不是换颜色，不是换方向，而是“同样开口方向下，输出辐射束宽度由墙色决定”。
    24	#   complexity_calibration:
    25	#     - 只保留两个档位 {1, 2}，避免颜色到连续参数的自由度过大。
    26	#     - 每个样例只用两种真墙色 {蓝, 红}，颜色种类少，视觉对比强。
    27	#     - 两个墙组件共用同一 fill 色，避免解题者误把差异归因于 fill 色。
    28	#   implicit_assumption_review:
    29	#     - 原代码 `wall = max(non_bg, key=count)` 依赖“真墙只有一种颜色”；变体中会把另一面真墙误判成 fill 或障碍，因此必须改成“按已知墙色集合逐个取大组件”。
    30	#     - 原代码 `other_colors = [c for c in non_bg if c != wall]` 默认只有一个墙色；变体里要同时排除蓝墙和红墙。
    31	#     - 原代码 `passable = (~barrier) & ((g == bg) | (g == fill))` 会把另一组件的 fill 种子也当作当前组件可通行区域；变体里改成“背景 or 当前 seed 组件”。
    32	#     - 原代码 `obstacles = ... & (g != wall)` 只排除一个墙色；变体里要只排除当前墙色，否则当前墙会在阴影扫描中把自己的辐射全部挡掉。
    33	#   placement_legality:
    34	#     - 生成器固定每个样例放两个墙，但把它们分配到不同半区：竖向模板用左右分区，横向模板用上下分区，避免填充束互相覆盖。
    35	#     - 两个墙复用同一个局部几何，减少“形状差异掩盖颜色差异”的风险，同时依然保留原题的随机 arm 细节。
    36	#     - 所有 seed 仍放在各自墙内、靠近闭口端，并继续用 solver 反查验证。
    37	#   observability:
    38	#     - 解题者在单个样例里就能看到蓝墙和红墙输出束宽不同；跨样例再看到颜色与宽度关系保持稳定。
    39	#     - 生成器额外拒绝“变体输出与所有墙都按 1 像素宽处理时完全相同”的样本，防止退化回原题。
    40	#   cleanliness:
    41	#     - 障碍数降低到少量单点，保留原题难点但不让画面变脏。
    42	#     - 两个辐射束被放在不同空间象限，避免覆盖层次过多。
    43	
    44	import random
    45	
    46	import numpy as np
    47	from scipy.ndimage import distance_transform_cdt
    48	
    49	from arc_utils import components_mask, get_bg, neighbors4, neighbors8
    50	
    51	
    52	RAY_WIDTH_BY_WALL = {
    53	    1: 1,  # blue wall -> thin boundary rays
    54	    2: 2,  # red wall -> thick boundary rays
    55	}
    56	WALL_COLORS = tuple(RAY_WIDTH_BY_WALL)
    57	WALL_COMPONENT_MIN = 14
    58	
    59	
    60	def _sgn(x: int) -> int:
    61	    return (x > 0) - (x < 0)
    62	
    63	
    64	def _degree1_pixels(points: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
    65	    pts = set(points)
    66	    return [
    67	        (r, c)
    68	        for r, c in pts
    69	        if sum((rr, cc) in pts for rr, cc in neighbors8(r, c)) == 1
    70	    ]
    71	
    72	
    73	def _wall_components(g: np.ndarray) -> list[dict[str, object]]:
    74	    comps: list[dict[str, object]] = []
    75	    for color in WALL_COLORS:
    76	        for pts in components_mask(g == color, connectivity=8):
    77	            comp = {(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts}
    78	            if len(comp) < WALL_COMPONENT_MIN:
    79	                continue
    80	            if len(_degree1_pixels(comp)) != 2:
    81	                continue
    82	            comps.append({"color": color, "points": comp})
    83	    return comps
    84	
    85	
    86	def _min_pair_dist(a: list[tuple[int, int]], b: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:
    87	    best = 10**9
    88	    for r, c in a:
    89	        for rr, cc in b:
    90	            d = abs(r - rr) + abs(c - cc)
    91	            if d < best:
    92	                best = d
    93	                if best == 0:
    94	                    return 0
    95	    return best
    96	
    97	
    98	def _fill_color(g: np.ndarray, bg: int, wall_comps: list[dict[str, object]]) -> int:
    99	    wall_points = [p for comp in wall_comps for p in comp["points"]]
   100	    non_bg = [int(v) for v in np.unique(g) if int(v) != bg]
   101	    other_colors = [c for c in non_bg if c not in WALL_COLORS]
   102	    assert other_colors, "expected at least one non-wall color"
   103	
   104	    def score(color: int) -> tuple[int, int]:
   105	        pts = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in zip(*np.where(g == color))]
   106	        best = 10**9
   107	        for r, c in pts:
   108	            for wr, wc in wall_points:
   109	                d = abs(r - wr) + abs(c - wc)
   110	                if d < best:
   111	                    best = d
   112	                    if best == 0:
   113	                        return 0, len(pts)
   114	        return best, len(pts)
   115	
   116	    return min(other_colors, key=score)
   117	
   118	
   119	def _comp_mask(shape: tuple[int, int], comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> np.ndarray:
   120	    mask = np.zeros(shape, dtype=bool)
   121	    for r, c in comp:
   122	        mask[r, c] = True
   123	    return mask
   124	
   125	
   126	def _comp_neighbors(r: int, c: int, comp_mask: np.ndarray) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
   127	    h, w = comp_mask.shape
   128	    out = []
   129	    for rr, cc in neighbors8(r, c):
   130	        if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and comp_mask[rr, cc]:
   131	            out.append((rr, cc))
   132	    return out
   133	
   134	
   135	def _wall_geometry(comp: set[tuple[int, int]], shape: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[list[tuple[int, int]], list[tuple[int, int]], list[bool], tuple[int, int]]:
   136	    comp_mask = _comp_mask(shape, comp)
   137	    endpoints = [p for p in comp if len(_comp_neighbors(*p, comp_mask)) == 1]
   138	    assert len(endpoints) == 2, "expected exactly two wall endpoints"
   139	
   140	    def outward_dir(ep: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], bool]:
   141	        n1 = _comp_neighbors(*ep, comp_mask)[0]
   142	        d1 = (_sgn(n1[0] - ep[0]), _sgn(n1[1] - ep[1]))
   143	        d_use = d1
   144	        is_12 = False
   145	        n2s = [p for p in _comp_neighbors(*n1, comp_mask) if p != ep]
   146	        if n2s:
   147	            n2 = n2s[0]
   148	            d2 = (_sgn(n2[0] - n1[0]), _sgn(n2[1] - n1[1]))
   149	            if (d1[0] == 0) ^ (d1[1] == 0):
   150	                if d2[0] != 0 and d2[1] != 0:
   151	                    d_use = d2
   152	                    is_12 = True
   153	        return (-d_use[0], -d_use[1]), is_12
   154	
   155	    out_info = [outward_dir(ep) for ep in endpoints]
   156	    out_dirs = [d for d, _ in out_info]
   157	    tip_12 = [flag for _, flag in out_info]
   158	    rad = (_sgn(sum(d[0] for d in out_dirs)), _sgn(sum(d[1] for d in out_dirs)))
   159	    return endpoints, out_dirs, tip_12, rad
   160	
   161	
   162	def _inward_offset(ep: tuple[int, int], endpoints: list[tuple[int, int]], rad: tuple[int, int]) -> tuple[int, int]:
   163	    if rad[0] != 0:
   164	        center = sum(c for _, c in endpoints) / len(endpoints)
   165	        return (0, 1 if ep[1] < center else -1)
   166	    center = sum(r for r, _ in endpoints) / len(endpoints)
   167	    return (1 if ep[0] < center else -1, 0)
   168	
   169	
   170	def _ray_points(start: tuple[int, int], d: tuple[int, int], rad: tuple[int, int], is_12: bool, shape: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
   171	    h, w = shape
   172	    rr, cc = start
   173	    pts = []
   174	    step = 0
   175	    while True:
   176	        step += 1
   177	        if not is_12:
   178	            rr += d[0]
   179	            cc += d[1]
   180	        elif step % 2 == 1:
   181	            rr += d[0]
   182	            cc += d[1]
   183	        elif rad[0] != 0:
   184	            rr += d[0]
   185	        else:
   186	            cc += d[1]
   187	        if not (0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w):
   188	            break
   189	        pts.append((rr, cc))
   190	    return pts
   191	
   192	
   193	def _apply_shadows(
   194	    out: np.ndarray,
   195	    g: np.ndarray,
   196	    filled_mask: np.ndarray,
   197	    obstacles: np.ndarray,
   198	    rad: tuple[int, int],
   199	    bg: int,
   200	) -> None:
   201	    h, w = g.shape
   202	
   203	    def shadow_process(coords: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> None:
   204	        started = False
   205	        blocked = False
   206	        for r, c in coords:
   207	            if filled_mask[r, c]:
   208	                started = True
   209	            if started and obstacles[r, c]:
   210	                blocked = True
   211	                continue
   212	            if blocked and filled_mask[r, c]:
   213	                out[r, c] = bg
   214	                filled_mask[r, c] = False
   215	
   216	    if rad == (0, 0):
   217	        return
   218	    dr, dc = rad
   219	    if dr != 0 and dc == 0:
   220	        for c in range(w):
   221	            rows = range(h) if dr > 0 else range(h - 1, -1, -1)
   222	            shadow_process([(r, c) for r in rows])
   223	    elif dc != 0 and dr == 0:
   224	        for r in range(h):
   225	            cols = range(w) if dc > 0 else range(w - 1, -1, -1)
   226	            shadow_process([(r, c) for c in cols])
   227	    elif dr == dc:
   228	        for k in range(-(w - 1), h):
   229	            coords = [(r, r - k) for r in range(h) if 0 <= r - k < w]
   230	            coords.sort(key=lambda rc: rc[0], reverse=(dr < 0))
   231	            shadow_process(coords)
   232	    else:
   233	        for k in range(h + w - 1):
   234	            coords = [(r, k - r) for r in range(h) if 0 <= k - r < w]
   235	            coords.sort(key=lambda rc: rc[0], reverse=(dr < 0))
   236	            shadow_process(coords)
   237	
   238	
   239	def _solve(grid: np.ndarray, ray_width_by_wall: dict[int, int]) -> np.ndarray:
   240	    g = np.array(grid, copy=True)
   241	    h, w = g.shape
   242	    bg = get_bg(g)
   243	
   244	    wall_comps = _wall_components(g)
   245	    assert wall_comps, "expected at least one wall component"
   246	
   247	    fill = _fill_color(g, bg, wall_comps)
   248	    fill_components = []
   249	    for pts in components_mask(g == fill, connectivity=4):
   250	        seed = [(int(r), int(c)) for r, c in pts]
   251	        if seed:
   252	            fill_components.append(seed)
   253	    if not fill_components:
   254	        return g
   255	
   256	    out = g.copy()
   257	    available = list(range(len(wall_comps)))
   258	
   259	    for seed_pts in fill_components:
   260	        candidates = available or list(range(len(wall_comps)))
   261	        wall_idx = min(
   262	            candidates,
   263	            key=lambda idx: (_min_pair_dist(seed_pts, wall_comps[idx]["points"]), -len(wall_comps[idx]["points"])),
   264	        )
   265	        if wall_idx in available:
   266	            available.remove(wall_idx)
   267	        wall_info = wall_comps[wall_idx]
   268	        wall_color = int(wall_info["color"])
   269	        wall_comp = wall_info["points"]
   270	        endpoints, out_dirs, tip_12, rad = _wall_geometry(wall_comp, (h, w))
   271	        barrier = _comp_mask((h, w), wall_comp)
   272	        width = ray_width_by_wall.get(wall_color, 1)
   273	
   274	        for ep, d, is_12 in zip(endpoints, out_dirs, tip_12):
   275	            inward = _inward_offset(ep, endpoints, rad)
   276	            for band in range(width):
   277	                start = (ep[0] + inward[0] * band, ep[1] + inward[1] * band)
   278	                if not (0 <= start[0] < h and 0 <= start[1] < w):
   279	                    continue
   280	                if band > 0:
   281	                    barrier[start] = True
   282	                for rr, cc in _ray_points(start, d, rad, is_12, (h, w)):
   283	                    barrier[rr, cc] = True
   284	
   285	        seed_mask = np.zeros_like(barrier, dtype=bool)
   286	        for r, c in seed_pts:
   287	            seed_mask[r, c] = True
   288	        passable = (~barrier) & ((g == bg) | seed_mask)
   289	        seen = np.zeros_like(passable, dtype=bool)
   290	        q = seed_pts[:]
   291	        for r, c in q:
   292	            if passable[r, c]:
   293	                seen[r, c] = True
   294	        while q:
   295	            r, c = q.pop()
   296	            for rr, cc in neighbors4(r, c):
   297	                if 0 <= rr < h and 0 <= cc < w and passable[rr, cc] and not seen[rr, cc]:
   298	                    seen[rr, cc] = True
   299	                    q.append((rr, cc))
   300	
   301	        filled_mask = seen & (g == bg)
   302	        out[filled_mask] = fill
   303	
   304	        obstacles = (g != bg) & (g != fill) & (g != wall_color)
   305	        _apply_shadows(out, g, filled_mask, obstacles, rad, bg)
   306	
   307	    return out
   308	
   309	
   310	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   311	    """
   312	    Fill each half-enclosed wall sprite and radiate it outward, with ray thickness determined by wall color.
   313	
   314	    Input structure:
   315	    - bg is the most common color. Blue and red 8-connected wall components are the true enclosure sprites.
   316	    - One shared fill-color seed blob sits inside each wall near its closed end; any other non-bg singletons are obstacles.
   317	
   318	    Rule:
   319	    - For every wall sprite, flood-fill the reachable interior and continue through the opening toward the outward direction inferred from the two endpoints.
   320	    - Blue walls emit the original 1-pixel boundary rays, while red walls emit 2-pixel-wide boundary bands by adding one inward parallel ray per side.

